# ~/.config/fedokawaii/backup-exclude — what kawa-backup leaves out of your home: ~/Downloads,
# caches, and what a program downloads again by itself. Everything else in your home is backed
# up. One pattern a line, restic's way: a path (the home filled in), or * for any name; a line
# starting with # is a comment. Changing it: in your working copy
# (configs/home/.config/fedokawaii/backup-exclude, then fedokawaii apply), never here — the
# theme writes this file.
# ~/Downloads: arrivals — torrents, ISO files, installers — big, and fetched again; it is
# outside the snapshots for the same reason (its own subvolume, §37.2). What you keep, move
# into ~/Documents and the like. To back it up as well, delete the line below
@HOME@/Downloads
@HOME@/.cache
@HOME@/.local/share/Trash
# uv's Pythons (setup and update make them), neovim's plugins and language servers (update
# fetches them, at the versions of ~/.config/nvim/lazy-lock.json, which is the desktop's own)
@HOME@/.local/share/uv
@HOME@/.local/share/nvim/lazy
@HOME@/.local/share/nvim/mason
# Prowlarr's container image (update pulls it again); its settings, ~/.config/prowlarr, stay in
@HOME@/.local/share/containers
# the desktop's release binaries and the wallpaper pack: update and Theme fetch them again
@HOME@/.local/share/fedokawaii/upstream
@HOME@/.local/share/fedokawaii/wallpapers
# the browser's caches (its bookmarks, passwords and settings stay in)
@HOME@/.config/net.imput.helium/*/Cache
@HOME@/.config/net.imput.helium/*/Code Cache
@HOME@/.config/net.imput.helium/*/GPUCache
@HOME@/.config/net.imput.helium/*/Service Worker/CacheStorage
@HOME@/.config/net.imput.helium/*/DawnGraphiteCache
@HOME@/.config/net.imput.helium/*/DawnWebGPUCache
@HOME@/.config/net.imput.helium/ShaderCache
# a backup of a backup: what restore put back is already in one
@HOME@/Restored
